  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/dburriss/orca",
  "published": "2026-09-03T05:47:52.957Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "`FetchReposState`'s two batches (`isArchived` and `search`, split in 0.10.3) now fetch their chunks concurrently instead of one at a time. Splitting the `search` batch down to 15 repos increased the number of sequential GraphQL round trips (e.g. 13 for 152 repos, up from 4); since this prefetch always runs single-threaded ahead of the per-repo fan-out regardless of `--parallel`/`--no-parallel`, running it sequentially made it the dominant cost of the whole run. Chunks are now dispatched with `Async.Parallel`, bounded/paced by the existing shared `ApiBucket` (which already rate-limits concurrent callers and pauses all of them together on a detected rate limit).",
  "repository": {
